From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:40:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] qcow2: wake the main loop of the driver thread on close

Since the queues have their own IOThread, the bh scheduled on each queue by
_qcow2_close() run in the IOThreads, and nothing wakes the main loop of the
td-qcow2 thread, which waits for driver_opened to change: closing any qcow2
image hung in qemu_thread_join().

Notify the main loop too.

Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
---
 drivers/block-qcow2.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/block-qcow2.c b/drivers/block-qcow2.c
index bd6dcfeb..2744aeb7 100644
--- a/drivers/block-qcow2.c
+++ b/drivers/block-qcow2.c
@@ -839,6 +839,11 @@ _qcow2_close(td_driver_t *driver)
 		struct qcow2_queue *q = &s->queue[qid];
 		qemu_bh_schedule(q->bh);
 	}
+	/*
+	 * The bh of the queues run in their IOThread: also wake the main loop
+	 * of the thread, which waits for driver_opened to change.
+	 */
+	qemu_notify_event();
 	pthread_mutex_unlock(&s->lock);
 
 	// Ignore return, qcow2_open() always return NULL; or will abort
